From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: The writer writes ASF files (6517)

BeginWriting was E_NOTIMPL and WriteSample/WriteStreamSample were
refused. A multiplexer written from the ASF specification now writes
the header (file properties, a stream properties object per audio or
video stream of the profile, the header extension, the content
descriptions of the writer's attributes), fixed-size data packets of
one payload each, and a simple index per video stream, to the output
file (whose header is completed at EndWriting) and to the writer's
sinks. WriteSample takes inputs whose format is the stream's own;
WriteStreamSample takes stream samples. The statistics count samples
and bytes. Also fixes the metadata editor (6515) freeing its attribute
store on Close while the program still held its IWMHeaderInfo.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
index dacead6..6f20a42 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
@@ -1,11 +1,12 @@
 MODULE    = wmvcore.dll
 IMPORTLIB = wmvcore
-IMPORTS   = kernel32 shlwapi
+IMPORTS   = kernel32 shlwapi ole32
 DELAYIMPORTS = winegstreamer
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
 SOURCES = \
+	asfmux.c \
 	async_reader.c \
 	editor.c \
 	profile.c \
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/asf.h b/dlls/wmvcore/asf.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f4d1a81
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/asf.h
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
